{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction from the real pinned-tool baseline: the old score table is not safe to gate current code. `signing.py` now generates 814 mutants (old record: 491). After roughly ten minutes at `--max-children 1`, 108 were still unchecked; 134 had survived and 348 were `no tests`. Inspection found both equivalents and a real contract gap (`_canonical_payload`: `\"v\"` -> `\"XXvXX\"` survived), so these cannot be bulk-fingerprinted. A single 30-minute base+head all-shard job is also not credibly bounded. Probe stopped before the next shard. We need to choose a rollout: differential baseline that blocks new regressions, narrower proven function scopes, or first remediate the existing survivor debt."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786423537669833001,"uuid":"68486aa6-22f9-442a-bd77-cd05a1160b47"}